This document defines long-term architectural horizons and advanced research milestones.
All future tracks align with the 10 strategic governance pillars and Boyd's E-M performance laws.
Active sprint tasks, the release state (v2.9.4), and near-term deliverables reside in ROADMAP.oot.

## 0. Strategic Architecture Alignment & Evolution Horizons

The openOODA technical horizon advances through four next-generation frontiers:
- Horizon 1 (Autonomous AI Swarm Mesh & MCP Federation): Decentralized peer-to-peer agent networks.
- Horizon 2 (Zero-Knowledge Verifiable Compute): Cryptographic STARK execution proofs for untrusted nodes.
- Horizon 3 (Direct Native Silicon Emission): Machine code generation for AArch64 and RISC-V.
- Horizon 4 (Live RASP & Boundary Physics Invariants): Real-time RAM memory protection and formal proofs.

## 1. Horizon 1: Autonomous AI Swarm Mesh & MCP Federation

- Byzantine Fault Tolerant Capability DAG Consensus (Pillar 6 Swarm Coordination):
  Coordinate heterogeneous agent swarms over a decentralized capability DAG.
  Authenticate inter-agent wire framing using Noise XX handshakes and ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD.
  Converge distributed sensor fusion and state transitions with sub-millisecond latency.

- Model Context Protocol (MCP) Swarm Federation:
  Federate capability graphs, tool registries, and memory trees across distributed agent clusters.
  Eliminate single-agent context saturation through decentralized gossip routing.

## 2. Horizon 2: Zero-Knowledge Verifiable Compute (ZK-STARKs)

- Cryptographic ZK Execution Proofs (Pillar 5 Capability Security):
  Pair SECRET field taint tracking with cryptographic ZK-STARK execution proofs.
  Execute `.oo` bytecode on untrusted cloud nodes with mathematical proof of contract compliance.
  Protect private data without exposing secret fields to untrusted hosts.

- Poseidon Algebraic Hashing & Quadratic Arithmetic Circuits:
  Lower `.oo` formal contracts directly into arithmetic circuits.
  Generate succinct verifiable computation proofs in linear time.

## 3. Horizon 3: Direct Native Silicon Emission

- Direct AArch64 & RISC-V Machine Code Emitters (Pillar 2 E-M Engine):
  Generate standalone Linux ELF64, macOS Mach-O, and bare-metal binaries without GCC/LLVM.
  Implement direct ARM NEON and RISC-V Vector (RVV) instruction encoders.

- Autonomic AST Mutator & Live PGO:
  Autonomous runtime fibers detect execution bottlenecks and mutate AST subtrees in memory.
  Transform Array-of-Structs to Struct-of-Arrays layout for maximum SIMD throughput.

## 4. Horizon 4: Live-RAM RASP & Boundary Physics Invariants

- Live-RAM Runtime Application Self-Protection (RASP Watchdog):
  Continuous memory integrity hashing detecting heap corruption and code injection.
  Automatic rollback to verified gold-master state upon memory tampering.

- Subtractive Drag Elimination:
  Enforce Landauer's Principle through linear arenas, bulk resets, and zero-leak ARC.
  Elide dynamic contract evaluations using compile-time SMT proof synthesis.
